# sourced by dhcpcd-run-hooks after every dhcpcd event (shared by Horcrux and Patronus server images).
# The hardware clock can be months off at boot (flat RTC battery, VM, fresh board) and chronyd starts before the link is up:
# it could not resolve its NTP pool and would only retry on its own back-off. On every bound lease tell chronyd the network
# is online, re-resolve its sources and take a quick burst of measurements, so makestep corrects the clock within seconds.
case "$reason" in
BOUND|BOUND6|REBOOT|REBIND|STATIC|INFORM|INFORM6)
	if command -v chronyc >/dev/null 2>&1 && [ -d /run/chrony ]; then
		( chronyc onoffline; chronyc reload sources; chronyc burst 4/4 ) >/dev/null 2>&1 &
	fi
	;;
esac
